 ### [Custom Perspective Projection Matrix Construction](2175-custom-perspective-projection-matrix-construction.md)
-This method constructs the perspective projection matrix for 3D rendering, specifically tailored for splat-based rendering pipelines where explicit control over focal lengths and aspect ratios is required. It solves the problem of mapping 3D view-space coordinates to 2D screen space by combining field-of-view (FOV) parameters with viewport dimensions, differing from fixed-function pipeline setups by allowing tangent-based FOV parameter management and explicit coordinate system conversions. It builds on [General Perspective Transformation](1845-general-perspective-transformation.md) by providing the specific matrix assembly logic used in modern splat renderers. See [Custom Perspective Projection Matrix Construction](2175-custom-perspective-projection-matrix-construction.md).
